WEBVTT

00:02.740 --> 00:04.480
<i>I'm Takahashi Misaki.</i>

00:05.070 --> 00:07.260
<i>A freshman studying economics at Mitsuhashi University.</i>

00:08.130 --> 00:12.460
<i>My brother, the only family I have, got married right when I started college,</i>

00:12.870 --> 00:15.110
<i>and he transferred to Osaka on top of that.</i>

00:16.590 --> 00:21.970
<i>It's been 6 months since I moved into the condo of my brother's best friend from high school,</i>

00:21.970 --> 00:27.940
<i>the great Lord Usami, a.k.a. Usagi-san, now an author and the recipient of both the Naomori and Kikukawa awards.</i>

00:31.850 --> 00:34.990
<i>I would say I have been living a pretty fulfilling life...</i>

00:36.010 --> 00:38.410
<i>...that's right... if not for this!</i>

00:40.690 --> 00:43.080
Wa-! ... Stop!

00:43.080 --> 00:44.360
Stop!

00:44.750 --> 00:48.440
<i>Somewhere along the way, Usagi-san and me... are like this...</i>

00:49.500 --> 00:51.680
<i>I could never tell this to my brother!</i>

00:52.040 --> 00:57.040
What happens once can happen twice

00:57.340 --> 01:02.590
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

00:57.340 --> 01:02.590
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

01:00.840 --> 01:14.110
Junjou Romantica 2

01:02.590 --> 01:06.060
ima futari no story

01:02.590 --> 01:06.060
Now, our story...

01:07.350 --> 01:14.840
bokura no mirai ga kagayaite yuku yo

01:07.350 --> 01:14.840
Our future is going to shine on.

01:18.280 --> 01:23.570
mae ni susumeba dareka to butsukatte

01:18.280 --> 01:23.570
If I try to move forward, I collide with someone else,

01:24.040 --> 01:28.400
okubyou ni naru bakari

01:24.040 --> 01:28.400
and always lose my nerve.

01:28.400 --> 01:34.000
dakedo mae wo muite aruite iku yo

01:28.400 --> 01:34.000
But I'm going to face front and walk ahead,

01:34.000 --> 01:37.630
kimi to aeru nara

01:34.000 --> 01:37.630
if it means I can see you.

01:39.660 --> 01:44.640
ame ni utarete furueru koe

01:39.660 --> 01:44.640
Your trembling voice, pelted by the rain,

01:44.970 --> 01:50.240
nemurenu yoru wo samayottemo

01:44.970 --> 01:50.240
even if I have to wander sleepless nights,

01:50.920 --> 01:53.720
boku wa yuku yo

01:50.920 --> 01:53.720
I'll go,

01:53.720 --> 02:00.470
kimi to deaeru sono hima de

01:53.720 --> 02:00.470
Until the day when I can see you.

02:01.290 --> 02:06.480
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

02:01.290 --> 02:06.480
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

02:06.480 --> 02:10.190
ima futari no story

02:06.480 --> 02:10.190
Now, our story

02:10.350 --> 02:12.000
ugokidashita

02:10.350 --> 02:12.000
has started.

02:12.000 --> 02:16.990
meguriatta shougeki de iro no nai sekai ga

02:12.000 --> 02:16.990
The impact of our meeting, shocked this dull, grey world

02:16.990 --> 02:24.180
isshun de azayaka ni irozuite yuku yo

02:16.990 --> 02:24.180
and instantly burst into a brilliant color.

02:28.240 --> 02:31.230
Usami-sensei! We've come to pick you up!

02:33.040 --> 02:35.270
<i>Nii-chan... this is the worst!</i>

02:37.080 --> 02:40.870
Let's go, right now, come on. I'll give you ten minutes.

02:40.960 --> 02:42.830
Get ready now, nice and quick.

02:43.030 --> 02:45.400
Isaka-san, you!

02:46.000 --> 02:49.100
Can't you see what I'm in the middle of right now?

02:49.360 --> 02:50.960
Hmm, let's see...

02:51.230 --> 02:54.570
Are you about to devour this young boy?

02:54.620 --> 02:56.310
You realize that and still linger around?

02:56.360 --> 02:57.540
I most certainly do.

02:57.840 --> 03:01.460
Anyway, just get yourself ready. The car's waiting outside.

03:01.520 --> 03:04.670
Huh? Where exactly are you hauling me off to?

03:04.820 --> 03:07.310
Where you ask? Isn't it obvious?

03:07.830 --> 03:12.450
Super novelist Usami Akihiko's Kikukawa Award celebration party!

03:12.560 --> 03:16.190
Hosted by Marukawa Publishing at Teito Hotel!

03:18.730 --> 03:20.320
Akihiko, why you!

03:20.400 --> 03:23.040
You're not getting out of this, not this time!

03:23.150 --> 03:26.700
Where and when exactly did who say they would go to?

03:26.890 --> 03:28.880
You don't have to do anything.

03:28.880 --> 03:32.130
Just give a little speech, flash that adorable smile of yours, spread some good cheer

03:32.130 --> 03:34.110
and everyone goes home happy.

03:34.150 --> 03:38.610
You know damn well that I hate doing that sort of thing the most!

03:41.180 --> 03:42.810
Aikawa-san!

03:42.980 --> 03:45.930
Misaki-kun! Let's eat lots of delicious food!

03:47.650 --> 03:49.460
The party itself is tomorrow.

03:49.560 --> 03:54.530
But for today, please make yourself right at home in an incredibly luxurious hotel suite!

03:54.620 --> 03:58.160
You'll have a 360 degree panoramic night view all to yourselves!

03:58.280 --> 04:00.360
Oh, how romantic~

04:02.070 --> 04:05.290
Do you really think you can reel me in with that?

04:05.730 --> 04:07.090
That's true.

04:07.090 --> 04:11.040
A hotel suite may not be anything new or exciting to you, but,

04:11.440 --> 04:14.630
what if that little cutie says he wishes he could go?

04:15.690 --> 04:20.060
Actually, I asked him once before, if he'd like to go with you.

04:20.350 --> 04:20.940
When?

04:21.220 --> 04:22.860
When you weren't around.

04:22.920 --> 04:26.080
He's such a good boy! Know what he said?

04:27.270 --> 04:30.310
Well, I don't get opportunities to go to places like that,

04:30.660 --> 04:32.400
so I'd like to go if I could.

04:32.750 --> 04:34.390
Usagi-san is always busy...

04:35.320 --> 04:37.170
and it'll be bad if I interfere...

04:37.940 --> 04:40.660
but if it's not with Usagi-san...

04:41.360 --> 04:42.810
It's boring...

04:44.980 --> 04:50.260
Hey, don't you want to show him a real gorgeous time once in a while?

04:50.470 --> 04:55.180
I think the little cutie will be really happy~

04:58.640 --> 05:00.650
Problem solved. Take care of the rest.

05:00.720 --> 05:02.440
You managed to persuade Usami Akihiko!

05:02.440 --> 05:04.300
That's the silver tongued Isaka for you!

05:06.400 --> 05:09.820
Ugh... I'm not so sure about this.

05:10.360 --> 05:12.830
I've never been to a party like this before.

05:13.030 --> 05:14.650
What am I supposed to do there anyway?

05:15.060 --> 05:18.920
Should I even be there at all in the first place?

05:19.070 --> 05:20.530
I'll definitely look out of place...

05:21.150 --> 05:23.280
I should have just turned down properly.

05:24.190 --> 05:26.000
Cutie, please!

05:26.080 --> 05:27.750
It's about Usagi-san, isn't it?

05:28.230 --> 05:29.690
It's none of my business.

05:30.320 --> 05:34.420
That guy... he's just got an ingrained prejudice against these kinds of things.

05:35.630 --> 05:38.950
But if you said you wanted to go, then he'll definitely go!

05:39.210 --> 05:39.980
Please!

05:40.060 --> 05:45.040
Actually, if he really doesn't want to go, I don't think it's good to force him.

05:45.420 --> 05:46.520
And also...

05:48.760 --> 05:51.330
Uh, Wh-What's wrong?

05:51.460 --> 05:55.770
This party is... really important for the company.

05:56.570 --> 06:01.290
Big-name writers, the literary greats, they're coming just for this party...

06:01.710 --> 06:06.850
If I can't even bring the leading man to his own party...

06:07.730 --> 06:10.000
I... I...

06:11.810 --> 06:14.320
I can't remain in this company!

06:16.000 --> 06:19.870
I got it! I'll go. It'll be fine if go, right?

06:24.570 --> 06:28.640
<i>I have this sneaking feeling that I got wrapped around
his little finger...</i>

06:31.950 --> 06:32.910
<i>Oh yeah!</i>

06:33.800 --> 06:36.520
<i>I haven't given Usagi-san any present yet.</i>

06:37.350 --> 06:40.350
<i>A bouquet is a little trite, but, you can't
go wrong with flowers.</i>

06:42.290 --> 06:44.110
<i>If it's about 3000 yen...</i>

06:48.610 --> 06:50.630
Um, excuse me!

06:50.780 --> 06:52.700
Yes, Welcome!

06:53.210 --> 06:57.060
Can I get a flower bouquet around 3000 yen?

06:57.180 --> 06:58.220
You can.

06:58.730 --> 06:59.770
Is it a present?

07:00.470 --> 07:01.190
Yes.

07:01.270 --> 07:03.520
<i>Huh!?...He's huge!</i>

07:03.590 --> 07:05.040
What kind would you like?

07:05.100 --> 07:06.830
Uh...

07:07.100 --> 07:09.880
Usagi-san

07:07.910 --> 07:09.880
Gorgeous

07:09.840 --> 07:11.970
Roses

07:13.260 --> 07:14.380
I'd like some roses.

07:14.860 --> 07:16.410
Okay, roses it is.

07:16.650 --> 07:17.420
Then...

07:21.250 --> 07:22.640
How about these?

07:23.220 --> 07:25.400
These roses are called Baby romantica.

07:25.750 --> 07:27.230
Y-Yes!

07:28.390 --> 07:29.890
<i>I wonder if he'll be happy...</i>

07:30.980 --> 07:34.400
<i>He got so many fancy things from other people too...</i>

07:38.930 --> 07:42.160
<i>Huh? What's up with him? Just standing there.</i>

07:43.180 --> 07:45.310
<i>It's crowded. Hurry up and buy one already.</i>

07:47.100 --> 07:47.580
<i>Huh?</i>

07:49.650 --> 07:50.240
Excuse me.

07:51.460 --> 07:53.520
If you want, I can check how much your stop is.

07:53.600 --> 07:54.080
Huh?

07:54.250 --> 07:57.940
Sorry, I thought maybe you couldn't see the train map.

07:59.470 --> 08:01.590
No, I can see it.

08:02.170 --> 08:04.850
I want to go to Teito Hotel.

08:05.200 --> 08:06.570
<i>The same as me...</i>

08:08.050 --> 08:11.840
Then, it's Hibiya Station, so that's 160 yen.

08:12.060 --> 08:12.770
I see.

08:16.500 --> 08:17.660
<i>Eh...!?</i>

08:19.360 --> 08:21.200
<i>Has this guy perhaps...</i>

08:22.550 --> 08:24.350
<i>...never been on a train before!?</i>

08:28.400 --> 08:32.520
I am going to Teito Hotel too. So if it's okay, should we go part of the way together.

08:42.530 --> 08:46.110
So... do you... not ride trains very often?

08:46.350 --> 08:50.700
That's right, a car always comes to pick me up.

08:51.070 --> 08:52.560
<i>He's rich!</i>

08:53.790 --> 08:56.790
<i>People like him really do exist!</i>

08:57.280 --> 09:00.050
<i>There aren't people like him around me...</i>

09:01.840 --> 09:02.330
<i>Ah!</i>

09:03.640 --> 09:04.410
<i>There is.</i>

09:04.980 --> 09:09.720
<i>Speaking of that, has Usagi-san ever ridden on a train?</i>

09:10.500 --> 09:13.160
<i>He's been on a bullet train and sleeper cars, but...</i>

09:13.670 --> 09:15.460
<i>I get the feeling that he's never set foot on the Yamate line.</i>

09:13.670 --> 09:16.300
<b>Note:</b> The Yama(no)te line is one of Tokyo's busiest and most important commuter rail lines.

09:26.720 --> 09:27.330
Here.

09:27.820 --> 09:30.170
Oh my. Thank you.

09:37.510 --> 09:39.860
Oh no, it's okay if you sit.

09:43.320 --> 09:46.600
Do you always give up your seat to people like this?

09:47.500 --> 09:50.240
No, its depends on the time, circumstances and the right timing...

09:52.110 --> 09:53.980
Do you like flowers?

09:55.090 --> 09:58.210
Oh no, this is a gift for someone else.

09:58.850 --> 10:01.090
But it's not like I hate them.

10:01.250 --> 10:05.770
Actually, I don't think anyone would be unhappy to receive flowers.

10:08.110 --> 10:08.990
Is that so.

10:11.380 --> 10:15.120
<i>Wow, this guy's... a little hard to talk to.</i>

10:17.590 --> 10:19.560
Usami Akihiko, recipient of the Kikukawa Award - "The Moon in the Box"

10:17.590 --> 10:19.560
Exciting news at Marukawa Shoten!!!

10:19.740 --> 10:20.570
<i>Awesome!</i>

10:20.820 --> 10:22.700
<i>Maybe I should take this poster as a keepsake.</i>

10:25.270 --> 10:27.080
Ah, wonderful, isn't he?

10:27.320 --> 10:29.780
Winning that prize has been a huge promotion for him.

10:29.880 --> 10:31.280
He's a boring writer.

10:33.310 --> 10:34.010
<i>What?</i>

10:34.810 --> 10:37.520
Ah... Have you read his books?

10:38.050 --> 10:39.490
They aren't worth reading.

10:40.670 --> 10:42.280
<i>What's with that?</i>

10:42.510 --> 10:44.570
<i>Well, everyone has likes and dislikes, but</i>

10:44.570 --> 10:47.960
<i>how can you say something is not worth reading
before you've even read it!?</i>

10:48.070 --> 10:50.770
<i>It's not like I'm trying to defend Usagi-san,</i>

10:50.770 --> 10:53.330
<i>but what's with that way of putting things.</i>

10:53.500 --> 10:57.410
<i>I mean, what's up with that attitude towards someone graciously
showing you the way...</i>

10:57.870 --> 11:00.740
<i>Ugh, though this and that aren't related...</i>

11:00.780 --> 11:02.730
<i>but you know, you know!</i>

11:03.020 --> 11:07.290
Next is Hibiya, Hibiya. Please exit on the left side of the train.

11:07.920 --> 11:10.000
<i>He kind of pisses me off!</i>

11:10.740 --> 11:12.840
Huh? Looks like it's not on this floor.

11:13.790 --> 11:16.910
That's because this hotel expanded recently.

11:17.140 --> 11:19.660
There's a separate building now. It's probably in there.

11:20.310 --> 11:23.300
Oh, then I'll go ask the front desk.

11:23.360 --> 11:24.530
Let's go together.

11:24.670 --> 11:27.900
Eh... Oh no, it's alright.

11:28.190 --> 11:28.810
Um...?

11:32.560 --> 11:35.690
Well, whatever. I should let Usagi-san know that I'm here.

11:41.220 --> 11:42.650
Ah, Usagi-san.

11:42.940 --> 11:45.040
It's me. Yeah, just got here.

11:47.680 --> 11:51.980
Oh! Whoa, it's you! Cool!

11:52.210 --> 11:54.060
Cutie! What a coincidence!

11:56.110 --> 11:58.580
Huh, ah, it's Haruhiko.

11:59.210 --> 12:00.330
Ryuichiro.

12:01.000 --> 12:02.480
What are you doing here?

12:02.610 --> 12:05.610
Work! See, this super novelist right here is...

12:05.610 --> 12:07.190
Why are you two together?

12:07.640 --> 12:10.470
Well, we kind of met as we were getting on the train,

12:10.760 --> 12:13.330
and we were heading to the same place, so...

12:14.110 --> 12:15.360
Huh? Is he your acquaintance?

12:15.670 --> 12:20.680
Rather than saying an acquaintance... this is Usami Haruhiko, Akihiko's elder brother.

12:34.410 --> 12:35.990
<i>Usagi-san's elder brother!</i>

12:36.020 --> 12:38.240
<i>This guy!? No way! Really?</i>

12:39.230 --> 12:43.490
<i>Now that you mention it, they do look a little alike, actually...</i>

12:44.310 --> 12:46.930
Did you get the day wrong?

12:46.930 --> 12:48.370
The party is tomorrow.

12:48.430 --> 12:50.310
Party? For what?

12:50.430 --> 12:53.150
What!? I sent you an invitation!

12:53.300 --> 12:54.700
Didn't you look at it?

12:54.700 --> 12:57.210
It's a celebration for Akihiko's award...

12:58.140 --> 12:58.890
Dunno...

12:59.430 --> 13:00.310
Hey now!

13:00.480 --> 13:04.050
I only came here for a meeting today.

13:04.600 --> 13:08.880
Never would have thought I'd run into you here.

13:10.470 --> 13:16.440
For the flowers you kindly sent the other day, Thank you very much.

13:17.110 --> 13:18.130
Flowers?

13:18.310 --> 13:21.760
Oh, my secretary must have sent those.

13:23.360 --> 13:25.570
I had nothing to do with it.

13:25.670 --> 13:26.820
<i>What's this...?</i>

13:26.820 --> 13:31.380
<i>The mood is kind of... scary!</i>

13:32.070 --> 13:34.250
<i>What?... Why?...</i>

13:35.810 --> 13:37.330
Misaki. Let's go.

13:37.800 --> 13:40.190
Isaka-san, I'll head up to the room first.

13:40.250 --> 13:41.140
Akihiko.

13:42.680 --> 13:45.530
When are you going to come back home?

13:47.050 --> 13:48.410
I won't be coming back.

13:48.800 --> 13:50.560
I've said this so many times!

13:51.280 --> 13:55.250
I left that house of my own will. I won't ask anything of it now.

13:55.400 --> 13:57.520
You all can do as you like.

13:57.570 --> 13:58.660
Stop messing around!

13:59.450 --> 14:06.110
It's your fault that I have to clean your mess, fill in the gap you left - you don't care about any of this do you!?

14:06.590 --> 14:08.590
If you don't want to do it, then don't.

14:09.360 --> 14:11.770
I haven't forced you to do anything.

14:12.000 --> 14:15.310
Easy for one to talk when they've bailed out and ran away.

14:15.530 --> 14:16.630
I suppose so.

14:16.950 --> 14:19.250
Hey now, both of you, cut it out!

14:19.250 --> 14:21.750
What did you run off to be? A novelist?

14:21.850 --> 14:22.800
Hey, Haruhiko!

14:22.870 --> 14:24.370
An enviable profession!

14:24.450 --> 14:28.950
To turn away from reality and occupy all of your time with daydreams and fantasies,

14:28.950 --> 14:30.950
what a wonderful life it must be!

14:31.210 --> 14:33.940
<i>What? Would someone say something like that normally?</i>

14:34.120 --> 14:36.430
Spewing page after page of worthless prose...

14:36.490 --> 14:37.340
<b>What?</b>

14:37.730 --> 14:40.220
...have them publish your trifling books,

14:40.320 --> 14:42.920
and on top of that, wallowing in self-complacency...

14:41.240 --> 14:42.290
What the hell?

14:43.570 --> 14:45.390
...must be quiet pleasant indeed!

14:45.580 --> 14:46.690
Shut up!

14:49.910 --> 14:51.210
What's with you?

14:52.980 --> 14:57.590
On the train just now, didn't you say you haven't read any of his books!?

14:57.840 --> 15:00.130
If you haven't read them, then stop mouthing off!

15:00.760 --> 15:04.200
You don't have the slightest idea how hard Usagi-san works to write his books!

15:04.740 --> 15:06.960
Sometimes he doesn't even sleep for a week!

15:07.430 --> 15:11.050
And Usagi-san's face at that time... how terrible it looks...

15:11.140 --> 15:12.870
...you haven't seen, have you!?

15:14.820 --> 15:17.590
Don't act like you know everything based on your own stupid assumptions!

15:17.690 --> 15:20.650
If you have any problem with him, why don't you read his book or two before you come to complain!?

15:22.320 --> 15:23.600
Moron!!

15:27.740 --> 15:29.640
Whoa, awesome!

15:30.220 --> 15:33.790
He's the only guy to call Usami Haruhiko a moron, since me.

15:33.840 --> 15:35.090
And did you see that?

15:35.910 --> 15:40.690
He flew into one hell of a rage, but was shaking like a leaf, his ears flopping down and his tail between his legs.

15:41.600 --> 15:42.930
Who was he?

15:43.250 --> 15:46.120
Akihiko's special someone, currently living with him.

15:46.320 --> 15:47.950
Together with Akihiko?

15:48.750 --> 15:49.550
Can't be...

15:50.020 --> 15:51.450
That's right...

15:51.530 --> 15:54.850
I too got quiet a shock when I heard it, seriously.

15:54.880 --> 15:58.560
He's really just a normal kid, nothing particularly striking about him...

15:59.020 --> 16:00.640
Oh, that's not correct,

16:01.290 --> 16:05.700
I guess being able to live with Akihiko is, in itself, an amazing talent...

16:08.060 --> 16:09.650
Really annoying!

16:09.700 --> 16:10.730
What was that!?

16:10.980 --> 16:12.830
Is that guy really your elder brother!?

16:13.230 --> 16:16.700
Even to your own brother, there are things to can and can't say!

16:16.730 --> 16:19.130
On top of that, was that any place to say such things!?

16:19.500 --> 16:21.150
Calm down, young man.

16:22.840 --> 16:24.530
How can I calm down!?

16:25.030 --> 16:27.250
Usagi-san, don't let it get to you!

16:28.340 --> 16:30.350
Your book was really interesting.

16:30.800 --> 16:32.590
Seriously, I'm not just saying that!

16:33.380 --> 16:37.750
I usually don't read books, but I read yours all the way till the end.

16:39.650 --> 16:41.000
I'm alright.

16:42.070 --> 16:45.040
It's been like that between us since long ago.

16:46.180 --> 16:49.200
It's the polar opposite of you and your brother, right?

16:53.170 --> 16:57.920
Um, Usagi-san... that is... how to say it best...

16:58.890 --> 16:59.660
...that is...

17:00.180 --> 17:04.350
I know I've talked about my brother a lot before.

17:05.000 --> 17:07.700
If that ever made you feel bad...

17:08.640 --> 17:09.730
...I'm sorry.

17:09.920 --> 17:14.380
Ah, no, if me saying this irritates you even more...

17:15.200 --> 17:16.610
...I'm even more sorry.

17:18.130 --> 17:23.520
I didn't really know anything about your brother, so...

17:29.220 --> 17:34.080
You're really always trying to be considerate of other people, aren't you?

17:35.140 --> 17:36.490
Why are you smiling?

17:37.160 --> 17:39.410
I was just thinking- Wow, Misaki is really angry.

17:40.360 --> 17:42.750
What? Is there anything funny about it?

17:42.880 --> 17:45.280
Stop smiling! I'm being serious here!

17:45.650 --> 17:47.400
I said stop smiling!

17:48.280 --> 17:50.680
I'm gonna go take a tour of the room to kill some time.

17:54.320 --> 17:58.880
What's this? They said it was a suite so I was expecting something really awesome!

17:59.090 --> 18:00.300
Are you dissatisfied with something?

18:00.910 --> 18:03.120
I mean there are no lions in the tub!

18:06.740 --> 18:08.750
What's with you from just now?

18:09.050 --> 18:13.840
You getting really angry for my sake made me really happy.

18:14.260 --> 18:14.940
Why?

18:15.710 --> 18:16.940
It wasn't anything special...

18:17.740 --> 18:18.760
I don't get it.

18:19.200 --> 18:19.830
Kid.

18:19.910 --> 18:20.920
What'd you say!?

18:21.450 --> 18:23.860
Oh, that's right, before I forget!

18:26.080 --> 18:27.250
Sorry it's late.

18:28.520 --> 18:30.640
It feels kind of super belated now, but...

18:30.960 --> 18:33.360
...I wanted to do this right.

18:34.590 --> 18:36.280
The book was really good!

18:37.050 --> 18:40.430
I just wanted to say it once more- Congratulations!

18:46.480 --> 18:48.030
What is it, so suddenly!?

18:48.270 --> 18:50.160
Let go of me! Stupid Usagi!

18:51.100 --> 18:55.500
I try so hard so say what I want, using so many words...

18:56.670 --> 18:59.000
but you don't need so many...

18:59.360 --> 19:01.600
Shut up. I'm just at high school Japanese level.

19:01.650 --> 19:02.980
That's not it.

19:04.160 --> 19:07.920
Saying less can convey much more sometimes.

19:08.970 --> 19:10.230
I don't get it.

19:10.280 --> 19:11.450
Because you're still a kid.

19:11.560 --> 19:12.380
What was that!?

19:13.020 --> 19:14.130
Don't make fun of me!

19:16.320 --> 19:19.010
Actually, I'm complimenting you.

19:24.720 --> 19:26.440
You really still are a kid.

19:27.030 --> 19:28.030
Shut up!

19:28.030 --> 19:29.130
So cute.

19:29.360 --> 19:30.930
Shut up, shut up!

19:31.320 --> 19:32.780
Don't treat me like a kid.

19:33.110 --> 19:35.840
Just wait and see, I've got a plan!

19:36.940 --> 19:41.400
One day, for sure, I'm seriously definitely going to take you on!

19:45.930 --> 19:48.980
You really are so cute.

19:52.410 --> 19:54.440
I'm sorry the flowers were so cheap.

19:55.050 --> 19:55.990
Why?

19:56.160 --> 20:00.430
Er, well, I was just thinking that something more gorgeous would have been much better...

20:01.150 --> 20:04.630
If it's something from you, I'm happy to get anything.

20:05.120 --> 20:07.760
I mean, you struggled with whether to give me flowers or not, right?

20:08.460 --> 20:09.570
Hm? Yeah.

20:09.900 --> 20:12.490
And you worried about if roses would be good or not, right?

20:13.480 --> 20:14.830
Hm? Yeah.

20:15.430 --> 20:17.850
That makes me happy.

20:18.430 --> 20:19.440
What does that mean?

20:19.650 --> 20:22.400
Well, anymore will be difficult for a kid.

20:23.380 --> 20:25.380
There you go treating me like a kid again!

20:26.680 --> 20:29.030
If it frustrates you then hurry up and become a man,

20:29.660 --> 20:31.450
and try "taking me on".

20:31.790 --> 20:33.020
I don't get it!

20:38.130 --> 20:41.250
<i>Did it really make him happy a little bit at least?</i>

20:42.560 --> 20:44.030
<i>If it made him happy, then...</i>

20:45.290 --> 20:49.660
<i>...that is... I'm really happy too.</i>

21:00.850 --> 21:05.990
Yokogiru dake wa ichinichi no owari ni

21:00.850 --> 21:05.990
Crossing paths at the end of the day,

21:06.120 --> 21:11.380
itsu kara ka kimi ga sakimawari shite matte ite

21:06.120 --> 21:11.380
at some point you went up ahead and waited for me.

21:11.730 --> 21:16.750
ureshii kimochi bai ni shite kurete

21:11.730 --> 21:16.750
You doubled all my happiness,

21:16.750 --> 21:23.440
kanamishi kimochi hanbun ni shite kureru kara

21:16.750 --> 21:23.440
and halved all my sadness.

21:23.550 --> 21:28.550
kore kara donna michi aruitemo

21:23.550 --> 21:28.550
No matter what path I walk in the future,

21:28.950 --> 21:33.230
kitto sore wa kimi he to tsuzuiteru

21:28.950 --> 21:33.230
will surely lead to you.

21:33.230 --> 21:35.990
boku no saki ni wa kimi ga ite

21:33.230 --> 21:35.990
You're there up ahead of me,

21:35.990 --> 21:38.850
kimi no saki ni wa boka ga iru

21:35.990 --> 21:38.850
I'm there ahead of you,

21:38.850 --> 21:44.120
hoka no dare mo inai futari dake no basho

21:38.850 --> 21:44.120
A place for just the two of us with no one else around.

21:44.120 --> 21:50.020
sore ga boku no subete nanda sore ga boku wo karuku shiteru na

21:44.120 --> 21:50.020
That's my everything, and lifts the weight off my shoulders.

21:50.610 --> 21:55.090
mou doko he mo ikanaide

21:50.610 --> 21:55.090
Hey, don't go anywhere.

21:55.090 --> 22:00.550
yakusoku no basho wa itsumo hidamari no kaori wo sasete

21:55.090 --> 22:00.550
Our promised place always has the smell of sunshine.

22:00.550 --> 22:05.940
boku no ashimoto wo terashiteirunda

22:00.550 --> 22:05.940
It's casting a light at my feet.

22:05.940 --> 22:11.760
kimi no koto ga suki da yotte to ieru boku ga suki dakara

22:05.940 --> 22:11.760
I love myself being able to say "I love you!"

22:12.150 --> 22:17.440
mune no oku de sotto arigatou

22:12.150 --> 22:17.440
Softly in my heart I say, "Thank you."

22:22.020 --> 22:25.310
Sensei..., what's with this mountain of suits?

22:25.310 --> 22:26.850
I bought them for you.

22:26.850 --> 22:27.760
Bought them!?

22:28.040 --> 22:29.290
All!? For me!?

22:29.980 --> 22:32.400
Wear whichever you like for the party tonight.

22:33.000 --> 22:36.550
But I just brought the one you bought for me before!

22:36.790 --> 22:38.300
A new one's always better.

22:39.650 --> 22:42.720
Return them! The receipts, where are the receipts!?

22:42.830 --> 22:44.080
There's no such thing.

22:44.220 --> 22:47.170
At least keep the ones for expensive purchases, you spendthrift novelist!

22:47.210 --> 22:49.880
I'll teach you a proper appreciation for money!

22:50.480 --> 22:55.490
Oh, right. I also had the bath lion catalogue delivered.

22:56.040 --> 22:56.640
Want to see?

23:02.570 --> 23:04.190
Room service!

23:04.370 --> 23:05.240
Oh, Hello.

23:05.290 --> 23:08.880
I also have these flowers for Takahashi Misaki-sama.

23:09.140 --> 23:13.090
Huh? Are you sure they aren't for Usami Akihiko?

23:14.100 --> 23:18.020
No. These were definitely to be delivered to Takahashi Misaki-sama.

23:18.960 --> 23:20.640
The sender is...

23:21.440 --> 23:23.770
...Usami Haruhiko-sama.

23:27.390 --> 23:28.080
Why?

23:28.380 --> 23:29.420
Who knows.

23:31.220 --> 23:33.830
<i>Nii-chan, it's a sign of a storm!</i>

23:33.830 --> 23:46.270
Raws: BDRIP (from nyaa.se)
Translation: aarinfantasy
